# BUGS

The length of a runtime array of buffer elements whose stride isn't a power of two is an integer division, which the Valhall backend does not select, so it refuses such a program by name; a power of two is a shift and compiles.
The core's pipelines read the heap in the fragment stage only, so a texture or sampler in a compute or vertex shader is lowered and then refused by the core.
`OpArrayLength` of a descriptor whose range is less than the array's offset gives a huge count, not 0.
An index into an array of buffers or images is not checked against the descriptor array's size.
The alignment promised to every access is the type's natural one (a `vec3` 16): a buffer address that is not that aligned is undefined.
